<title>SINGAPORE: Mobil Singapore considers cutting refinery runs.</title>
<headline>Mobil Singapore considers cutting refinery runs.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Singapore may soon join the three other refiners in cutting throughputs at its 280,000 barrels-per-day refinery, company sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>Sources said the marketing and refinery departments were currently considering run cuts because of weak refining margins.</p>
<p>&quot;It is definitely a possibility,&quot; one source said.</p>
<p>He said Mobil's planned shutdown of the whole refinery mid-March was too far forward to affect the decision to reduce throughputs.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
